00:09:49.147 --> 00:09:49.980
- I just wanted to be 90 pounds.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.910
That was it, that was my mark
of success as a human being.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:53.660
Or just like basic worth.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:57.241
And so I started campaigning
against the fashion industry

00:09:57.241 --> 00:10:00.050
and I entered the fashion
industry in order to do it.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.060
I became a model scout.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:03.120
I started trying to scout plus sized girls

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.583
but I was ahead of the curve,

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:07.290
no pun intended,

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:10.910
and so I used to so they said
no to all of the curvy girls

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.300
but I started writing letters to magazines

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.180
about what I was seeing

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:16.260
and they were making 12 year
olds cry about their weights

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.400
and I kicked off the size zero debate

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.650
with a letter that I wrote to
the Evening Standard in the UK

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:22.840
and it turned into this
huge thing across the news.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.090
I was all over the news.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.706
I was doing live Channel 4.

00:10:25.706 --> 00:10:28.010
This was in England and BBC Live.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:30.734
I was 19 years old, there's
still little videos of this

00:10:30.734 --> 00:10:32.463
on Getty images.

00:10:33.931 --> 00:10:36.120
I've been talking about
everything I'm talking about now

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.500
for the longest time.
- [Gary] Good for you.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.270
- The dumbest thing about what's going on

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:40.220
in my career right now

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.040
is that I have the majority support,

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.320
like I say 90% support.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:45.930
But the 10% of people who
give me a lot of shit--

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.950
- We're talking about macro
feedback from the world.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:48.783
- [Jameela] Yeah.

00:10:48.783 --> 00:10:50.396
- [Gary] Social articles.
- Social media,

00:10:50.396 --> 00:10:51.229
People.
- Understood.

00:10:51.229 --> 00:10:52.250
- [Jameela] I have massive support--

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.640
- I understand it's 90/10.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.880
- When people try to take me down,

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.050
they treat me as someone who a year ago

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.160
was an actress in The Good Place

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.703
who just decided to pick up activism

00:11:00.703 --> 00:11:02.570
because I thought it would make me trendy

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.050
because activism has become trendy.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.260
It's like I have been in
this shit for 14 years.

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.703
Some of you little haters
weren't even alive.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.920
- You know, this is something
I can connect with you on.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.570
How do you think about that

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.410
because you're bringing it up now.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.480
So I have empathy for that.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.670
Makes sense to me.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:24.760
Don't you love though that
the truth is on your side?

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.480
I think for me, the thing that,

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.130
you know and I kind of
live this life as well.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:30.122
Right now I'm kind of getting destroyed.

00:11:30.122 --> 00:11:31.176
- [Jameela] Are you?
- Currently,

00:11:31.176 --> 00:11:33.050
in certain pockets because

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:35.410
I think sometimes its
strategic to do free work

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:36.700
to get your foot in the door,

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.992
which makes me you know,
a complete vampire.

00:11:38.992 --> 00:11:41.010
No free work ever.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.660
Obviously--
- We've all done that.

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:47.690
- I think so but many people
who have not had to do that

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.550
who did not grow up the way I did,

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:50.649
who don't realize

00:11:50.649 --> 00:11:52.640
they think they're
fighting for other people

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.700
but what they're actually doing is showing

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:56.630
their unbelievable privilege

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.600
of never having to be in that scenario

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.820
do not agree with that.
- It's an audition process.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:01.653
It's an audition process,
that's what it is.

00:12:01.653 --> 00:12:04.130
- I will do it until the day I die,

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.620
I'm not always looking for a check

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.793
in return for why I'm doing something.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:11.420
I mean, you sat here and talked about

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:12.480
the thing I believe in the most,

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.230
which is a platform where you have

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:15.734
awareness to be able to do something.

00:12:15.734 --> 00:12:19.300
The attention is the number one thing.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.920
And yet, so nonetheless,
but it hurts my feelings.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.997
People are like, "You're the devil."

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.341
It makes me, I'm a human.

00:12:27.341 --> 00:12:32.341
However, when people are
like, when they say anything,

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:36.480
and we all will be,
judgment is way more trendy.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.313
- Oh we're just addicts.

00:12:37.313 --> 00:12:39.970
- Then activist, then anything.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:42.850
Judgment is the fucking number
one thing that's happening

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:43.960
in society at scale.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.670
As a matter of fact, I'm
actually a little bit,

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:47.553
actually I'm bouncing around here.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:49.770
- I'm actually weirded out--
- [Jameela] My ADD

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.470
can follow this, you just can't move

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.354
or make any sounds like--

00:12:52.354 --> 00:12:54.330
I'm with you Gary.
- So how about this?

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:55.540
Right here, you ready?

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.932
How about this: I'm actually
scared that we are on such

00:12:57.932 --> 00:13:00.820
hyper attack and judgment
that what we do as humans,

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.850
always is counteract the other way

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:06.030
and I find myself now, honestly,

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:07.777
I was DNA-wise and parenting-wise I was--

00:13:07.777 --> 00:13:11.780
- You think you're being pushed
back into archaic beliefs

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:14.290
because you're fed up at the,

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:15.870
you're like, "Get back into the kitchen."

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.460
- No.
- [Jameela] I'm joking.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:21.600
- But the fact that you're
making that connection

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:22.770
does get me to a point.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:25.522
I'm so sad that everyone's
judging everyone

00:13:25.522 --> 00:13:29.100
on an adjective during a conversation,

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.691
not even a debate amongst
acquaintance friends,

00:13:31.691 --> 00:13:33.290
that I'm concerned

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.340
because I understand
how humans are wired--

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:37.830
- It's going to bring our defense up.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:39.560
- I'm at a point where I'm struggling to

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:40.880
judge anybody about anything.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:41.840
It's actually this weird,

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.020
kind of like reverse thing that scares me,

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:46.053
that it's the chess move to the bad stuff.

00:13:46.053 --> 00:13:47.853
I'm like the macro is going play out.

00:13:47.853 --> 00:13:50.780
So nonetheless, I'm ranting
because you're bringing

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:53.640
a lot of thoughtful fodder
to me and I like it.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.666
This is the kind of shit
I like talking about.

00:13:55.666 --> 00:13:58.539
- My way of dealing with this
is that I was just like--

00:13:58.539 --> 00:14:01.090
- You have truth on your
side is where I'm going.

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:02.632
- A, I have truth on my side.
- [Gary] Period.

00:14:02.632 --> 00:14:04.980
- No but, there is always a B.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:06.760
I'm also a flawed human being.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:07.610
I'm gonna make mistakes.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.443
I've made mistakes.

00:14:08.443 --> 00:14:10.670
I have receipts of mistakes that I've made

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.080
because the internet never forgets.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.790
And so what I've had to do is

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.698
just accept that some people are right

00:14:15.698 --> 00:14:17.420
when they are criticizing me.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:19.425
They are right and they
have a right to criticize me

00:14:19.425 --> 00:14:21.870
and I don't take it personally
anymore because I can't.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.000
Because if you're going to be an activist,

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.797
you have to leave your ego
and your pride at the door

00:14:24.797 --> 00:14:25.630
and so I've just realized that

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.550
if I'm going to put myself out there,

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.890
and put my opinions all over the place,

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:30.830
I have to be willing to

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:32.550
take some shit back and it just doesn't.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:33.600
I'm not here to be liked.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.560
I couldn't give a fuck about being liked.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.393
I'm not interested in it.

00:14:36.393 --> 00:14:38.220
I've come here to create change

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:40.340
so no one ever goes through
what I've been through.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.530
- [Gary] I understand.
- Ever again.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.190
So I don't really care about that.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:46.904
But also, I have decided
to make it part of my,

00:14:46.904 --> 00:14:49.839
I'm going to say the word, brand.

00:14:49.839 --> 00:14:51.300
But I've decided to make
it part of my brand.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:54.290
- Can I help you with brand for a second?

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.153
On your throw up?

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.650
I'm so fascinated by societies.

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:00.280
- [Jameela] I am English
though, we are assholes.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.113
- Respect.

00:15:03.248 --> 00:15:05.348
And English and London is part of society.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:10.200
I'm fascinated by the semantics of words.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.980
People are unbelievably
throwing up on each other

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:14.332
about personal brand or brand,

00:15:14.332 --> 00:15:19.332
yet if you just say reputation,
it's remarkably consumable.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:24.480
I am scolded if I even go down
the path of the word hustle,

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.980
for being a bro.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.400
Yet, if I change it to work ethic,

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.360
I'm admired for acknowledging that

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.710
it's part of the equation.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:34.590
Semantics of words, back to judgment,

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:37.200
has become fucking ridiculous.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.450
- But brand is infused
with capitalism as a word.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:42.270
It's marinated in the idea of capitalism.

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.000
- [Gary] So say reputation.
- Yeah fine.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.823
But my whole shtick,

00:15:46.823 --> 00:15:48.170
shall I say.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.003
Am I saying shtick?

00:15:49.003 --> 00:15:49.877
No.
- [Gary] Shtick's very good.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.854
I like shtick, that's
very comfortable with me.

00:15:52.854 --> 00:15:55.200
- It's that I am a flawed person

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.360
and the thing that I
constantly say to people

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:58.430
throughout my activism is

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.380
we are looking for
progress, not perfection.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:03.030
The hunt for moral purity
will never go anywhere

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:04.100
because it doesn't exist

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.690
and also human beings continue to update.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.560
We have to continue updating
ourselves, like iPhones,

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:12.240
and we have to keep
learning about new genders,

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.710
new sexualities, new ways
in which people want to live

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:16.950
and we have to learn how to unlearn

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.680
our previous programming around that

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.930
and get with the program now.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:23.220
And so I very much so own,

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:26.080
my pinned tweet is all of my mistakes.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.550
So I'm just like, "Come at me bro."

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.143
Like I'm not hiding from my flaws.

00:16:30.143 --> 00:16:31.610
- It's the last scene of Eight Mile.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.873
I bring it up all the time.
- [Jameela] Yeah.

00:16:32.873 --> 00:16:34.280
It's the best way to play.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:35.390
- Exactly and so I'm just.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.150
- [Gary] I got it, that's awesome.

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:38.346
- It doesn't bother me.

00:16:38.346 --> 00:16:39.330
- By the way, it's fucking amazing.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:40.860
- [Jameela] Thanks.
- It makes you happier.

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:44.980
- It's also made my, it's
helped my career as an actor

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.390
weirdly because more men
follow me than ever before.

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.400
More people who've made mistakes

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.180
find that my social media
is a safe space to learn

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.580
because now we've made
people too afraid to

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:56.490
even put their hand up and
say, "I don't know the answer."

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:57.323
- 100%.

00:16:57.323 --> 00:16:58.900
- We chastise people for ignorance.

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:00.290
You can't chastise someone for something

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.080
that they don't even know yet

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.690
and so you can chastise someone for

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.190
deliberate, willful ignorance.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.680
- You can when you are delusional

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:10.683
and you start getting into
this ideological place.

00:17:10.683 --> 00:17:11.516
- [Jameela] That's what I'm saying.

00:17:11.516 --> 00:17:12.440
Willful ignorance and you're not--

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.060
- We completely lack empathy.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:15.810
We completely, collectively lack empathy.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.570
- [Jameela] Yeah, yeah.
- We cast judgment

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:19.450
through our filter.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:20.684
- [Jameela] Make no space for trauma.

00:17:20.684 --> 00:17:24.461
- Any, any compassion or empathy at all.

00:17:24.461 --> 00:17:25.560
- [Jameela] Or nuance, yeah.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.245
- It's ridiculous.

00:17:27.245 --> 00:17:28.630
- And so look, willful
ignorance is the only one that

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.560
I think you can chastise people for

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:31.940
because there's always
an ability to learn.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:32.773
We have the internet.

00:17:32.773 --> 00:17:34.460
You've got no excuse
if you live in the west

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:35.780
and you have the internet on your phone,

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.660
you have no excuse not to not update

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.527
your own information every single day.

00:17:38.527 --> 00:17:39.830
- Putting your head in the
sand because you choose to.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:40.663
- Yeah.

00:17:40.663 --> 00:17:41.570
- Looking the other way

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:43.050
because it's in your vested interest.

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.550
- [Jameela] Exactly.
- I completely agree with you.

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:46.480
- So that's my, that's where I'm at

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:48.590
and it's been very helpful
to me in my career.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:49.430
- What else do you like?

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:53.127
Do you like food, music, sport,

00:17:53.127 --> 00:17:56.500
like just for five seconds
from my own curiosity.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.333
- I love food.

00:17:57.333 --> 00:17:58.194
- What about board games?

00:17:58.194 --> 00:17:59.400
- I love food, I love board games.

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:00.233
- What is your favorite board game?

00:18:00.233 --> 00:18:01.066
- Scrabble.

00:18:01.066 --> 00:18:02.630
- Because you're fucking
great at it because you're a

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:03.900
fucking writer?
- [Jameela] Yeah.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.590
- Fuck, I can't spell for shit.

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:06.494
I like to know, never.

00:18:06.494 --> 00:18:09.970
Like I play Scrabble and I get dominated

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:10.997
and my friend will look over and is like,

00:18:10.997 --> 00:18:12.390
"Why didn't you make the word cat?"

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:13.320
I'm like, "Fuck."

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.780
Like I'm the worst.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:15.770
What about Monopoly?

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.550
- You're doing okay in other areas Gary,

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:18.440
so I'm not worried about you.

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:19.680
- By the way, it's really fascinating,

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.810
it took me a long, long time,

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:22.710
because of the '80s,

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:24.905
because my mother was
embarrassed of her accent

00:18:24.905 --> 00:18:26.820
so she wouldn't go to school nights

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:28.215
because a lot of things that happened,

00:18:28.215 --> 00:18:30.900
a lot of the things
about myself I now know,

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:32.539
I had to learn much, much, much later.

00:18:32.539 --> 00:18:35.730
I will go and speak in Madison
Square Garden right now

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:37.630
in front of 35,000 people right now.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:38.463
If you're like, "You have to go do it."

00:18:38.463 --> 00:18:39.396
In a heartbeat.

00:18:39.396 --> 00:18:43.130
If you ask me to read the
first page of that comic book,

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:44.360
I would shrivel.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.092
This goes all the way
back to those things.

00:18:46.092 --> 00:18:49.750
But to your point, I'm
also wildly observant

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.700
and it's because the way I learn

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.670
wasn't through words.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:54.800
- No, same.
- [Gary] You know?

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.050
- Yeah, I had difficulty reading.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.170
I had difficulty reading music

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:59.147
and yeah, I could play
at a grade eight level

00:18:59.147 --> 00:19:01.080
but I can't read any music.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.088
I have trouble ingesting
information via written word.

